{"id":"R0038","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"","evidence":[["E1","PDF",3,"B. System Model","We split the CNN architecture into four logical components","Primary system paper describing a Docker Swarm and Redis distributed CNN architecture."],["E2","PDF",5,"A. Experimental Setup","a pair of UAVs running on Raspberry Pis","Evaluated testbed explicitly represents two mini-UAVs on Raspberry Pi 5 nodes with base-station replicas."],["E3","PDF",2,"II. RELATED WORK","fragmenting the CNN model into its architectural layers","CNN layers are explicitly partitioned across UAV nodes and synchronized via Redis for collaborative inference."],["E4","PDF",5,"B. Experimental Results","average inference time per CNN layer operating independently","Prototype evaluation on 100 images reports per-layer inference latency, accuracy, and node-loss recovery."],["E5","https://www.wincom-conf.org/WINCOM_2025/?page=submission",0,"News","2025-12-31","IEEE Xplore effective posting 2025-12-31 within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26; event date 25-27 November 2025."],["E6","PDF",2,"II. RELATED WORK","CNN models require substantial computing resources to perform","Full 6-page report body is in English."],["E7","https://www.wincom-conf.org/WINCOM_2025/?page=submission",0,"Submission","All submitted papers will go through a peer review","Official WINCOM 2025 submission page confirms peer review for this 6-page IEEE conference paper."]]}
{"id":"R0052","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Each UAV executes standalone onboard perception rather than distributed or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"III. METHODOLOGY","the proposed framework leverages a modular drone-swarm system","Primary conference research paper presenting a multi-UAV framework and simulation validation."],["E2","PDF",5,"B) Defensive Swarm Configuration","comprises 10 quadrotor UAVs, each equipped with simulated","Evaluated multi-UAV topology explicitly contains 10 quadrotor UAVs in AirSim and ROS 2."],["E3","PDF",3,"A) System Overview and Architectural Design","Each drone independently performs perception","Each UAV runs a standalone onboard ViT locally while DRL coordinates swarm roles; no distributed DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",5,"A) Simulation Environment","developed in a hybrid simulation setup integrating Microsoft AirSim","Evaluated in simulation with baseline comparisons and ablation experiments."],["E5","sources/raw/core_searches/ieee_xplore_complementary_export_2026-11-26.csv",0,"Online Date","21 Jan 2026","Supplied publisher export physical row 18 Online Date 21 Jan 2026 within window; separate from 28-30 Oct. 2025 event and Crossref print date."],["E6","PDF",2,"A) Swarm Intelligence in Autonomous Aerial Systems","Swarm intelligence has gained traction in UAV applications","Full 8-page report body is in English."],["E7","https://pspb.ieee.org/images/files/PSPB/opsmanual.pdf",0,"Section 8.2.2.B.1","10.1109/ICCES67310.2025.11337136","IEEE conference proceedings DOI linked with IEEE PSPB Operations Manual §8.2.2.B.1 peer-review rule; no file acquisition rights inferred from DOI."]]}
{"id":"R0106","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","we consider a multiple UAV (MUAV)-enabled ISCC network","Primary journal research article proposing a split-learning collaborative inference and MA-DRL framework."],["E2","PDF",3,"III. SYSTEM MODEL AND PROBLEM FORMULATION","which consists of M UAVs, N single antenna","Evaluated system explicitly models and simulates a multi-UAV network of cooperating UAVs."],["E3","PDF",4,"A. SL-Enabled GTST Inference Scheme","different NN blocks are inferred on different W-UAVs","Pre-trained DNN layers are partitioned into multiple blocks and inferred sequentially across working UAVs."],["E4","PDF",10,"V. SIMULATION RESULTS","effectiveness and performance superiority of the proposed scheme","Numerical simulations evaluate the proposed split-inference method against multiple benchmark schemes."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footnote","Date of publication 3 June 2025","First publication 2025-06-03 on p1 and Codex-verified supplied date at https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1109/twc.2025.3573654; issue date November 2025."],["E6","PDF",2,"II. RELATED WORKS","The UAV-enabled ISCC networks have been extensively studied","Full 15-page journal article body is in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Footnote","associate editor coordinating the review of this article","Physical p1 documents received/revised/accepted dates and associate editor review for this peer-reviewed IEEE journal article."]]}
{"id":"R0145","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"","version_note":"ACM Just Accepted author manuscript (nonfinal copy; not final typeset issue version).","evidence":[["E1","PDF",6,"3.1 System Overview","each UAV is equipped with a small LLM","Primary journal article proposing an LLM-based cloud-edge UAV swarm path planning and continual learning system."],["E2","PDF",14,"6.1 Experiment settings","The UAV swarm consists of 10 UAVs","Evaluated multi-UAV topology explicitly consists of 10 UAVs."],["E3","PDF",16,"6.2 Performance Comparison of Different LLMs","DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B and LLaMA-3.2-3B as the cloud-side and","Models LLM inference time/FLOPs and distributes LLM inference requests across cloud large LLM and onboard UAV small LLMs in a hybrid scheme."],["E4","PDF",17,"6.2 Performance Comparison of Different LLMs","uniformly compared the communication time, inference time, and","Extensive experiments compare 7 LLMs, 3 cloud-edge inference schemes, and 2 baselines across 20 scenarios."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3774655",0,"published-online","2025-11-03","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2025-11-03 within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26; Just Accepted 2025/11."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 INTRODUCTION","multiple UAVs are often deployed in swarms to","Full 22-page journal manuscript body is in English."],["E7","PDF",22,"Publication history","Received 23 June 2025; revised 6 September 2025","Physical p22 documents peer-review revision and acceptance (22 October 2025) in ACM TAAS."]]}
{"id":"R0220","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Implements factor-graph WLS and EKF cooperative navigation with no DNN/CNN/SNN/VLM/LLM inference workload.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",5,"2.3 Factor Screening Method","this paper proposes an efficient distributed cooperative navigation","Primary conference paper proposing a factor-graph screening method for UAV swarm navigation."],["E2","PDF",5,"3.1 Simulation Experiment Design","The UAV swarm consist of 196 fixed-wing MAV","Evaluated setting explicitly simulates a swarm of 196 fixed-wing UAVs."],["E3","PDF",4,"2.3 Factor Screening Method","we use Weighted Least Squares (WLS) algorithm to","Uses factor-graph WLS and EKF positioning with no neural inference; p7 Conclusion defers AI algorithms to future work."],["E4","PDF",5,"3.1 Simulation Experiment Design","simulation flight duration is 500s, and each experiment","Monte Carlo simulations (100 runs) compare 3 navigation algorithms on RMSE and computation time."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3727993.3728075",0,"published-online","2025-05-26","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2025-05-26 within window; event date December 06-08, 2024."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","The algorithm based on factor graph has an","Full 8-page report body is in English."],["E7","https://www.acm.org/publications/icps/apply",0,"Conference Guidelines","at least two positive reviews required to approve","ACM ICPS policy mandates peer review, but edition-specific CMSDA 2024 CFP/track peer-review clause was not verified."]]}
{"id":"R0223","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"3 Methods","We propose a loop intelligent control framework called UTTUT","Primary conference paper proposing UTTUT, P^3 factor graph, and improved PPO with LLM and multimodal perception."],["E2","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","obstacle avoidance tasks of 3-6 UAVs, achieving path","Evaluated setting explicitly tests 3 and 6 UAVs in MATLAB and multi-UAV teams in AirSim."],["E3","PDF",5,"4.2 Multi-Agent Cooperative Task Planning Experiments","compare centralization, parallelism, distribution, and master frameworks shown","Explicitly distributes and compares server LLM/VLM (Doubao-1.5-pro/vision-pro) and drone-side Grounding DINO inference across 4 topologies."],["E4","PDF",5,"4.2 Multi-Agent Cooperative Task Planning Experiments","Each task is executed at least 30 times","Quantitative MATLAB and AirSim experiments measure success rate, path length, response time, and completion time."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3760269.3760299",0,"published-online","2025-09-17","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2025-09-17 within window; event date June 06-08, 2025."],["E6","PDF",2,"2 Relative work","Path planning for multi-agent UAV systems has become","Full 8-page report body is in English."],["E7","https://www.acaib.org/EditorialPolicy",0,"Editorial Policy","assigned to reviewers for double-blind peer review","Official ACAIB Editorial Policy confirms double-blind peer review by 2-3 independent reviewers for full ACM proceedings papers."]]}
{"id":"R0228","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Evaluates a multi-UAV digital twin with standalone RPi power/latency profiling only; defers offloading evaluation to future work.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","have developed a Digital Twin (DT) System named GazeboNS3","Primary workshop paper introducing a coupled Gazebo, ArduPilot SITL, and NS-3 digital twin."],["E2","PDF",5,"5 EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS","networking delays and packet losses by using two UAVs","Evaluated setting uses 2 UAVs for network tests and up to 10 UAVs for scalability."],["E3","PDF",6,"6 CONCLUSION","plan to use this DT system to evaluate","Only standalone single-board Raspberry Pi classification latency/wattage is profiled for battery modeling; no collaborative DNN inference is evaluated."],["E4","PDF",6,"5 EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS","the simulation performance remains stable up to 10 drones","Evaluates packet loss/delay, position sync error, battery drain, and multi-UAV scalability."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3711875.3737659",0,"published-online","2025-09-25","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2025-09-25 within window; event date June 23-27, 2025."],["E6","PDF",2,"2 RELATED WORK","Our work is based on three foundational open-source components","Full 6-page report body is in English."],["E7","https://sites.google.com/view/dronet2025/",0,"IMPORTANT DATES","Paper submission: April 19th May 4th, 2025","DroNet 2025 organizer page lists submission and decision dates but no explicit peer-review clause; parent MobiSys CFP does not establish workshop policy."]]}
{"id":"R0229","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Federated learning training for local wind-aware trajectory optimization only; no distributed or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"2.1 System architecture","consists of three main components: local learning units deployed","Primary conference paper proposing an FL-based wind-aware trajectory optimization framework."],["E2","PDF",4,"3 EXPERIMENTAL SETUP","In each experiment, five UAVs complete ten mission rounds","Evaluated setting explicitly simulates a 5-UAV swarm."],["E3","PDF",2,"2.1 System architecture","Each UAV observes local flight states, trains a local","Uses FedAvg federated training for local A* trajectory cost prediction rather than collaborative or distributed DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",4,"4.1 Energy reduction","The FL-based optimizer reduces the average energy consumption","Python simulations across 20 runs evaluate energy savings, wind sensitivity, and differential privacy trade-offs."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3838457.3838477",0,"published-online","2026-09-14","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2026-09-14 within window; event date May 15-17, 2026."],["E6","PDF",2,"2.1 System architecture","The proposed system consists of three main components","Full 7-page report body is in English."],["E7","https://www.acm.org/publications/icps/apply",0,"Conference Guidelines","at least two positive reviews required to approve","ACM ICPS policy mandates peer review, but an opened official IoTML 2026 edition CFP/track peer-review clause was not directly verified."]]}
{"id":"R0230","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Federated learning training and weight aggregation only; no collaborative or distributed DNN inference across UAVs.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","developed a comprehensive framework that integrates FL techniques","Primary conference paper evaluating an FL pipeline for drone swarms on the AERPAW testbed."],["E2","PDF",3,"3.1 AERPAW Experiment Configuration","The setup encompasses 2 to 5 portable nodes","Evaluated testbed explicitly uses 2 to 5 portable drone nodes with a fixed aggregator node."],["E3","PDF",4,"3.2.1 FL Preliminaries","Flower orchestrates the distributed training process by coordinating","Implements federated learning training and central model aggregation rather than distributed or collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",7,"4.1 Evaluation Framework","we extend the measurement workflow with custom Python","Evaluated on AERPAW measuring ML, hardware, and network performance metrics."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3700838.3700857",0,"published-online","2025-01-04","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2025-01-04 within window; event date January 04-07, 2025."],["E6","PDF",2,"2.1 AERPAW Testbed","AERPAW offers a comprehensive infrastructure for conducting experiments","Full 11-page report body is in English."],["E7","https://cse.iith.ac.in/icdcn-2025/call_for_paper.html",0,"Double-Blind Reviewing","employ a lightweight double-blind reviewing process","Official ICDCN 2025 Call for Papers confirms double-blind peer review for full conference papers."]]}
{"id":"R0231","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluates stationary IoT devices and HAPs rather than a multi-UAV topology, using generic bit-level offloading with PPO as optimizer.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",3,"1 Introduction","we propose a cooperative multi-split and multi-hop stochastic","Primary journal article proposing the c2mec multi-split, multi-hop edge task offloading framework."],["E2","PDF",6,"3.1 Two Timescales Optimization","targets a subset of IoT devices characterized by stationary","Evaluates 8 stationary HAPs and 26-38 stationary IoT devices; no evaluated multi-UAV topology."],["E3","PDF",7,"3.1 Two Timescales Optimization","indicates the amount of data generated by IoT device","Splits generic bit-level workloads (bits and CPU cycles/bit) using PPO solely as an offloading optimizer; no explicit DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",19,"7 Performance Evaluation","we show simulation results to validate the schedulability","Simulations over 1,000 time periods compare 6 offloading and DRL algorithms."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3772281",0,"published-online","2026-08-24","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2026-08-24 within window; issue date September 2026."],["E6","PDF",4,"2.1 Multi-hop Task Offloading","The multi-hop task offloading problems have been studied","Full 28-page journal article body is in English."],["E7","PDF",28,"Publication history","Received 2 November 2024; revised 3 May 2025","Physical p28 documents peer-review revision and acceptance (7 October 2025) in ACM TECS."]]}
{"id":"R0232","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":[],"reason":"Evaluates individual single-board UAV computers offloading to one UGV laptop rather than an evaluated multi-UAV topology.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",3,"3 OBJECT RECOGNITION OFFLOADING","propose two methods to identify the region for offloading","Primary workshop paper proposing SSIM-based and BING-based object recognition offloading."],["E2","PDF",4,"4 EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS","Raspberry Pi 4 Model B, a Jetson Nano, and","Benchmarks 3 SBC platforms individually against 1 UGV laptop over WiFi; no multi-UAV topology or multi-UAV interaction is evaluated."],["E3","PDF",5,"4.2 Performance Comparison with Baselines","The laptop runs the YOLOv7 model on GPU","Explicitly evaluates partial and full offloading of YOLOv7 object recognition inference from UAV onboard computer to edge laptop."],["E4","PDF",4,"4.2 Performance Comparison with Baselines","compare the following metrics: energy consumption of RPi and","Hardware experiments on 3 drone videos compare SSIM, BING, local YOLOv7-tiny, and full offloading."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3597060.3597240",0,"published-online","2023-06-19","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2023-06-19 within window; event date June 18, 2023."],["E6","PDF",2,"2 RELATED WORK","The two most popular classes of algorithms for","Full 6-page workshop paper body is in English."],["E7","https://dronet2023.github.io/",0,"Submission Intructions","DroNet follows a single-blinded review process","Official DroNet 2023 site lists this exact report as Article #6 and confirms single-blinded peer review."]]}
{"id":"R0234","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Models generic bit-level task offloading using KAT-MAPPO as optimizer with no explicit DNN/CNN/VLM/LLM inference workload evaluated.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",3,"1 Introduction","We propose a novel Kolmogorov-Arnold Transformer-based MAPPO","Primary journal article proposing KAT-MAPPO and analytical resource allocation for Cloud-Edge-Ground task offloading."],["E2","PDF",15,"5.1 Simulation Settings","served by 3 UAV edge servers and a cloud","Evaluated topology explicitly includes 3 UAV edge servers serving 12 ground devices plus a cloud server."],["E3","PDF",5,"3.1 Task and Computation Model","required number of CPU cycles to execute a","Models generic divisible bit workloads (Mbits, cycles/bit) and uses KAT-MAPPO solely as an offloading optimizer; no explicit DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",14,"5 Performance Evaluation","evaluate the training performance and system performance during training","Simulations compare KAT-MAPPO against 4 baselines across training, multi-seed, suburban, and rural scenarios."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3844610",0,"published-online","2026-09-23","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2026-09-23 within window; issue date November 2026."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","Task offloading has emerged as a key component for","Full 23-page journal article body is in English."],["E7","PDF",23,"Publication history","Received 14 October 2025; revised 4 June 2026","Physical p23 documents peer-review revision and acceptance (22 August 2026) in ACM TOIT."]]}
{"id":"R0238","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Centralized single-workstation knowledge-graph subgraph matching with no evaluated multi-UAV topology or distributed DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"3.2 Formal Definition of Dynamic Event Graph","The dynamic event knowledge graph can be formalized","Primary conference paper proposing a dynamic knowledge graph and two-stage subgraph matching framework."],["E2","PDF",5,"6.1 Experimental Environment and Dataset","this study employs a simulation-generated scenario dataset","Evaluates 700 simulated air-defense scenarios on one workstation; multi-UAV appears only as a target pattern category, not a multi-UAV topology."],["E3","PDF",5,"6.1 Experimental Environment and Dataset","NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 GPU, 16 GB RAM","Runs centralized single-machine spatiotemporal GNN and CSP/VF3 matching with no distributed or collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",5,"6.2 Comparison Methods and Metrics","all five methods were evaluated on the same 700","Evaluates accuracy, F1, NDCG, MAE, latency, and throughput against 4 baselines plus ablation study."],["E5","https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3821725.3821803",0,"published-online","2026-09-16","Codex-verified supplied date: publisher-deposited published-online 2026-09-16 within window; event date April 10-12, 2026."],["E6","PDF",2,"3.1 Situational Awareness Element Ontology Design","the ontology is structured into six entity categories","Full 6-page report body is in English."],["E7","https://www.acm.org/publications/icps/apply",0,"Conference Guidelines","at least two positive reviews required to approve","ACM ICPS policy mandates peer review, but an official MLNN 2026 edition CFP/track peer-review clause was not opened and verified."]]}
